 | `AMP_DATA_DIR` | Override the root directory, or comma-separated root directories, containing Amp data |
 | `LOG_LEVEL`    | Adjust verbosity (0 silent ... 5 trace)                                               |
 
+## Duplicate snapshots
+
+Matching event or message IDs within one thread count once when their usage fields agree. All selected roots take part in that check. Numeric and string message IDs stay distinct. Ledger cache attachments must also agree.
+
+Conflicting usage, overlapping snapshots without stable IDs, or mixed ledger/message snapshots fail the Amp report. One snapshot without IDs still works. The loader does not choose a winner from file order, modification time, or the greatest count. Different thread IDs stay separate. This does not resolve copied fork history across threads.
+
+The scan fails when selected files or folders cannot be read. Damaged JSON and usage without a thread ID also fail. Valid metadata without usage remains skippable. An absent default Amp folder returns no usage. Each explicit root must exist and be a directory. A non-UTF-8 root setting fails instead of selecting the default home.
+
 ## Troubleshooting
 
 ::: details No Amp usage data found
